package io.godstone.mesh.readiness

// T38 readiness court (android isle) -- the twin of ReadinessT38Tests.swift.
//
// One signed SOS envelope: keep the outer SOS code and required flags and the
// canonical signature rule (section 15). The vectors of
// crypto/sos_v1_vectors.json (schema 1, generated by
// crypto/gen_sos_v1_vectors.py) are the single source of truth for BOTH
// isles: each court reads the same file at runtime (the T07 repo-root
// idiom), so transcription drift between the benches is impossible by
// construction. The loader is deliberately minimal and fail-closed: the
// fixture is this repository's own artifact in the generator's known
// two-space layout; any vector missing a required member raises at once.
//
// The witnesses are the card's named cases: cross-platform author/verify
// (W1), zero signature (W2), changed key/body/msgID (W3), fake SOS via a
// one-bit type change (W4), malformed binding (W5), public-key-to-identity
// binding with the authenticated key distinguished from the verified person
// (W6), bounded UTF-8 body (W7), duplicate logical SOS (W8), the unknown-
// time pairing (W9), composed authorship through MeshNode (W10) and the
// inbound relay truth with unauthenticated frames never promoted (W11).
// Every assertion is positive and expected; the observer counters and the
// store's held-set census are the oracles that make the five named
// falsifications killable (accept-structure-only, transcript-without-magic,
// msg-id-over-signed-span, trust-claimed-node, skip-required-flags).

